  "pieces_note": "head = the angular crested great helm with the cross visor (front only), rigid; torso with the leather cowl, scarf, cross strap, round bronze buckle and BOTH pauldrons fused in (rigid; the pauldrons sit over the shoulder joints, so no pauldron pixel may belong to an arm: the arms swing beneath them); pelvis with the broad belt and square buckle fused in; loincloth = the deep-red front loincloth (front view) as a skinned cloth chain on pelvis (loincloth_mid, loincloth_tip; at most 3 px follow-through); loincloth_back = the back loincloth (rear view; its hem also shows between the legs in the front) as a skinned cloth chain on pelvis (loincloth_back_mid, loincloth_back_tip; at most 3 px follow-through); per arm a skinned root limb over upper and fore with the plate gauntlet as a rigid hand; falchion = the curved blade, crossguard, leather-wrapped grip and pommel as one rigid held item in hand_far (the sword hand is the far hand in the front and the near-camera right hand in the rear; follow the maquette's part labels, which name it hand_far in both views), pivot at the grip; per leg a skinned root leg (cuisse, knee cop with its side wing, greave) and a rigid sabaton. Hidden fills (spec 1, the rr-37/rr-42/rr-44 lesson): every area a moving arm, gauntlet, falchion or loincloth uncovers must show its covered piece's own painted continuation (torso flanks and belly under each arm's full motion footprint, the front loincloth and thighs under the near gauntlet, the far thigh and flank under the falchion arm). Report those regions as masks; the director paints the underlays.",
